### Checklist

- [x] I have searched for related issues but did not get the expected help.
- [x] This bug has not been fixed in the latest version.
- [x] Please note that if your bug description lacks corresponding environment information and a minimal reproducible demo, it will be difficult for us to reproduce and resolve the issue, which may reduce the possibility of receiving feedback, or even lead to the issue being closed.

### 🐞 Detailed Description of the Problem

**Summary.** The account page renders three things outside the translation table, so in the English UI the credit ledger still shows Chinese labels, Chinese `万` number formatting and `zh-CN` dates.

**Steps to reproduce**

1. Switch the interface language to `English` (`设置 › 通用 › 界面语言`).
2. Open the account page (rail avatar → account) and look at the credit metrics and the ledger rows.

**Observed** (`645dc7ba`, code reading; the page itself renders from these helpers)

```ts
// apps/desktop/src/views/AccountPage.tsx:93
function formatTokens(value: number): string {
  return value >= 10_000 ? `${(value / 10_000).toFixed(value >= 100_000 ? 0 : 1)}万` : formatNumber(value);
}
// :109
function bizLabel(type: string): string {
  const labels: Record<string, string> = {
    REGISTER: "注册赠送", CHECKIN: "每日签到", BONUS: "累计签到奖励",
    LLM_USAGE: "模型调用", ADMIN: "人工调整", REFUND: "退还",
  };
  return labels[type] ?? type;
}
// :104
function formatTime(iso: string): string {
  return Number.isNaN(date.getTime()) ? "—" : date.toLocaleString("zh-CN", { hour12: false });
}
```

Used at `:481` (`formatTokens(tokenEstimate)`), `:533` (`bizLabel(row.bizType)` + `formatTime(row.createdAt)`) and `:599` (`TEXT.account.signedInAt(formatTime(...))`). The same page's other strings do come from `TEXT.account.*` (`en.ts:196-232` already has "Available credits", "Credit activity and spending", "No credit activity yet."), so only these three helpers stay Chinese.

**Root cause.** The page keeps a few formatters local instead of taking the language from `useLanguage()` / `TEXT`; `formatNumber` at `:61` and `formatCredits` at `:69` also hardcode `toLocaleString("zh-CN")`.

**Expected.** In the English UI: thousands-separated numbers (or `K`/`M`), English ledger labels ("Sign-up bonus", "Daily check-in", …) and a locale-appropriate date format. The fix is one helper each: take the locale from the language context and add the label keys to both `zh.ts` and `en.ts`.

**Impact**

- The English UI is otherwise translated; the account page is the one screen that reads half-Chinese, which looks like a broken build.
- `1.2万` is unreadable for a user who does not read Chinese numerals, and the ledger's business types are the only explanation of where credits came from.
- Dates formatted `zh-CN` render as `2026/11/25 14:00:00`, which is ambiguous next to English labels.

### Detailed Environment Information Description

- ScienceDiscovery desktop client (English UI), source `645dc7ba3dde868bf7dcdc6f674e937d42284d3a`.
- Found by reading `apps/desktop/src/views/AccountPage.tsx`; not reproduced in a running client (the test host was unavailable at the time).

### Additional Information

- The three helpers are the only hardcoded Chinese strings in `apps/desktop/src` outside the text tables besides the export filename fallback and the default account name (reported separately).

### Version Information

- `openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery` @ `645dc7ba3dde868bf7dcdc6f674e937d42284d3a` (main, 2026-11-25).

issue:1404.body:
### Checklist

- [x] I have searched for related issues but did not get the expected help.
- [x] This bug has not been fixed in the latest version.
- [x] Please note that if your bug description lacks corresponding technical details and a minimal reproducible demo, it will be difficult for us to reproduce and resolve the issue, which may reduce the possibility of receiving feedback, or even lead to the issue being closed.

### 🐞 Detailed Description of the Problem

**Summary.** The skill editor carries its own byte formatter, and it is worse than the shared one the app already uses: a package one byte under a mebibyte reads `1,024 KB` there (the exact `1024KB` spelling the shared helper documents having fixed), and its numbers are formatted in the operating system's locale rather than the app's.

**Steps to reproduce**

1. `设置 › 技能` → open a skill whose package is just under 1 MiB (SKILL.md plus resources, e.g. ~1,048,000 bytes).
2. Compare the `已用 … / 64 MB` line with the same size in `会话 › 导出会话` (the research-package dialog).

**Observed** (`645dc7ba`)

```tsx
// apps/desktop/src/views/settings/SkillEditorView.tsx:98-104
function formatBytes(bytes: number): string {
  const mb = bytes / (1024 * 1024);
  if (mb >= 1) return `${new Intl.NumberFormat(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: 1 }).format(mb)} MB`;
  const kb = bytes / 1024;
  if (kb >= 1) return `${new Intl.NumberFormat(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: 1 }).format(kb)} KB`;
  return `${bytes} B`;
}
```

`1_048_000` bytes → `mb = 0.999_…` (below 1, so no promotion) → `kb = 1023.4` → formatted with one decimal → `1,024 KB`. The shared helper does the opposite, because it promotes on the *printed* number:

```ts
// apps/desktop/src/app/format-bytes.ts:18-24
const print = (value: number): number => Number(value.toFixed(1));
export function formatBytes(bytes: number): string {
  if (!Number.isFinite(bytes)) return "—";
  const { unit, value } = sizeInUnit(Math.max(0, Math.round(bytes)), print, PACKAGE_SIZE_UNITS.length);
  return `${unit === 0 ? Math.round(value) : value.toFixed(1)} ${PACKAGE_SIZE_UNITS[unit]}`;
}
// → "1.0 MB" for the same 1,048,000 bytes
```

Two further consequences of the local copy:

- `Intl.NumberFormat(undefined, …)` follows the **OS** locale, so on a German or French machine the package line reads `1,5 MB` / `1 023 Ko`-style separators while the rest of 设置 is in the interface language (the app has `TEXT.languageTag` for exactly this).
- The editor's thresholds are `>= 1`, not the shared ladder, so `1_073_741_823` bytes prints `1,024 MB` instead of `1.0 GB`.

**Root cause.** A fifth copy of "bytes as a human size" lives in a view component. The repository already has `app/format-bytes.ts` (`formatBytes`), `app/attachments.ts` (`formatFileSize`), `views/WorkspacePanel.tsx` (`formatWorkspaceSize`) and `views/SetupWizard.tsx` (`formatFreeSpace`), and `size-units.ts` exists specifically to make the unit follow the printed number. The editor's copy predates or ignores it.

**Expected.** The editor uses `formatBytes` from `app/format-bytes.ts`. If its ladder really should differ (it should not — the same package is shown by the export dialog), that would be a `sizeInUnit` caller, not a new function.

**Impact**

- The page whose whole job is "does this package still fit the 64 MB limit" prints the size in a scale that crosses its own unit boundary: `1,024 KB` reads as twice `1.0 MB` to anyone scanning for the limit.
- The same package is spelled three ways across the app (`1,024 KB` here, `1.0 MB` in the export dialog, `1024.0 KiB` in the workspace panel), so sizes cannot be compared between screens.
- The number is locale-formatted from the OS while every label around it follows the interface language, which is the same mismatch reported separately for timestamps.

### Detailed Environment Information Description

- ScienceDiscovery desktop client, source `645dc7ba3dde868bf7dcdc6f674e937d42284d3a`.
- Derived from `apps/desktop/src/views/settings/SkillEditorView.tsx:98-104` (call sites `:538-539`, `:617`) and `apps/desktop/src/app/format-bytes.ts:18-24`; not reproduced in a running client (the test host was unavailable at the time).

### Additional Information

- `size-units.ts` documents the failure mode by name: "Reading the unit off the unrounded value is what printed `1024KB`, `1024MB` and `1024 MiB`". The skill editor is that bug, still present, in the one place that is not a research package.
- `PACKAGE_LIMITS.totalBytes` is formatted by the same local function, so the denominator of the quota line goes through the same two problems.

### Version Information

- `openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery` @ `645dc7ba3dde868bf7dcdc6f674e937d42284d3a` (main, 2026-11-25).

issue:1474.body:
### Checklist

- [x] I have searched for related issues but did not get the expected help.
- [x] This bug has not been fixed in the latest version.
- [x] The description below carries environment information and a minimal reproducible demo.

### Detailed Description of the Problem

**现象**：在 `idea-tree` 的「继续」这条命令上，只要 evolve 侧的命令应答超过 15 秒（或应答丢失），API 会把刚发给该研究的 LLM 凭证撤销，而引擎已经在跑。结果是：用户看到「继续」失败，研究却被真的重新启动了，随后每一次模型调用都被 401 打回，研究以失败收场。

**这不是猜测，链路每一段都能指到行：**

1. `services/api/src/idea-tree/research.ts:61-64`：`continue` 时先 `tokens.revoke(researchId)`，再 `tokens.issue(...)`，并记为 `issued`。
2. `services/api/src/idea-tree/research.ts:73-76`：发往 evolve 的命令带 `AbortSignal.timeout(15_000)`。
3. `services/evolve/src/sciencediscovery_evolve/vendor/idea_tree/research_service.py:178-194`：`start()` **先** `asyncio.create_task(drive())` 把引擎跑起来，**再**返回；`:240` 的 `continue` 就是调它。
4. 于是 15 秒超时（或应答中途丢失）时：引擎已在跑，但 API 走进 `research.ts:84-86` 的 `catch`，`options.tokens.revoke(issued)` 并 `grants.delete(issued)`。
5. `services/api/src/evolution/llm-proxy.ts:133-140`：凭证被撤销后 `tokens.resolve()` 返回 `undefined`，LLM 代理直接 401 `Unauthorized`。

**最小可复现 demo**（只用仓库里的真实模块 `createIdeaResearchClient`；evolve 用一个故意慢 16 秒应答的假服务；store 与 token 注册表是桩）：

```ts
// repro.ts —— 在已装好依赖的 checkout 里运行：npx tsx repro.ts
import { createServer } from "node:http";
import { setTimeout as sleep } from "node:timers/promises";
import { createIdeaResearchClient } from "./services/api/src/idea-tree/research.ts";

const RESEARCH_ID = "research-1";
const SESSION = { id: "s1", projectId: "p1" };
let engineStarted = false;
const NOW = "2026-11-27T02:00:00.000Z";
const view = (status: string) => ({
  graph: { edges: [], nodes: [], objective: "repro", revision: 1, treeId: "tree-1", updatedAt: NOW },
  research: {
    batch: [], batchCompleted: 0, id: RESEARCH_ID, modelId: "m1", objective: "repro",
    phase: "building_tree", reason: null, round: 1,
    settings: { candidatesPerRound: 3, maxActiveDirections: 3, maxDepth: 5, maxNodes: 20, maxRounds: 8, maxSearchRounds: 10, pruneMinAssessments: 2, pruneScoreGap: 0.1 },
    status, tokens: 0, usageKnown: true,
  },
});

const server = createServer(async (request, response) => {
  let body = "";
  for await (const chunk of request) body += chunk;
  const payload = JSON.parse(body || "{}");
  if (payload.operation === "continue") {
    engineStarted = true;      // start() 已经把引擎调度起来
    await sleep(16_000);       // 应答晚于 API 的 15s 超时
  }
  response.writeHead(200, { "content-type": "application/json" });
  response.end(JSON.stringify(payload.operation === "list" ? { items: [view("paused")] } : view(payload.operation === "continue" ? "running" : "paused")));
});
await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.listen(0, "127.0.0.1", resolve));
const port = (server.address() as { port: number }).port;

const issued = new Set<string>();
const tokens = {
  issue: (runId: string) => { const token = `token-${runId}-${issued.size + 1}`; issued.add(token); return token; },
  revoke: (runId: string) => { for (const token of [...issued]) if (token.startsWith(`token-${runId}-`)) issued.delete(token); },
  resolve: (runId: string, presented: string | undefined) => (presented && issued.has(presented) ? { runId } : undefined),
};
const store = {
  assertSessionWritable: () => SESSION, getModel: () => ({ id: "m1" }), getModelApiToken: () => "model-token",
  getSession: () => SESSION, resolveIdeaTreeSettings: () => ({}),
  resolveRuntimeSettings: () => ({ effective: { modelId: "m1" } }),
};
const client = createIdeaResearchClient({ apiOrigin: "http://127.0.0.1:1", store: store as never, tokens: tokens as never, url: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}` });

let error = "";
try { await client.command("s1", "continue", { researchId: RESEARCH_ID }); } catch (reason) { error = reason instanceof Error ? reason.message : String(reason); }

const stillValid = [...issued].some((token) => token.startsWith(`token-${RESEARCH_ID}-`));
console.log(JSON.stringify({ apiSawError: error, engineStarted, grantStillValid: stillValid }, null, 2));
client.close();
server.close();
```

实际输出（本机 2026-11-27 11:20 跑的一次）：

```json
{
  "apiSawError": "The operation was aborted due to timeout",
  "engineStarted": true,
  "grantAlive": false,
  "revoked": [
    "token-research-1-1"
  ]
}
```

`engineStarted: true` + `grantAlive: false` 就是这次 bug 的核心：引擎在跑，凭证没了。同一形状也适用于 `create`（`research.ts:42` 的 `operation === "create"` 分支走同一段发放与 catch）。

**触发条件说明（不夸大）**：需要这条命令的应答超过 15 秒或中途丢失。evolve 侧 `command` 是单事件循环上的同步文件读写（`research.py:147-161` 每次 `save()` 都 `fsync` + 原子替换），大研究或慢盘时会变慢；本次 demo 只是把这个时延固定成 16 秒来稳定复现。

**建议修法**：`catch` 里不要直接撤销刚发的凭证，而是先 `get` 一次核对——研究已经是 `running` 就保留（或重新发放）凭证并如实告诉调用方「命令已生效但应答超时」；只有确认没跑起来才撤销。这样失败路径不会制造「在跑但没有凭证」的研究。

### Detailed Environment Information Description

- 仓库：`openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery`，审计基线 main `13f32dd5dd417283a397363496f0cae4f67326cb`（2026-11-27）
- 复现运行环境：WSL Ubuntu（`/home/yuanz/sciencediscovery`，已 `pnpm install`），Node + `tsx`；复现只依赖 `node:http`、`node:timers/promises` 与仓库内模块
- 未启动真实栈、未改动任何已安装实例；复现是进程内的，不触碰真实数据目录

### Additional Information

- 同一段代码在 `create` 上一致，若 `create` 的应答超时，会出现「研究已建、状态 running、凭证已撤销」的孤儿研究；重启后才会被 `reconcile_orphaned_researches()` 收成 `interrupted`。
- 相关但不同的一个问题（未提交 issue，先记录）：`http/index.ts:3463/3468/3819` 的清理是 `void ... .catch(log)`，删除会话时若清理失败，该会话的 grant 会留在注册表里，兜底 sweep 对已删会话 `getSession` 抛错后也退不掉，直到进程重启。
- 复现脚本已按最小化原则只保留必要分支；如需我把它整理成 `services/api/src/idea-tree/research.test.ts` 里的一个用例，我可以直接提 PR。

### Version Information

- 源码：`13f32dd5dd417283a397363496f0cae4f67326cb`（main，2026-11-27）
- 桌面端安装包：`C:\sd-daily\packages\ScienceDiscovery-20261127-9e91f78.exe`（0.4.0，来自 `9e91f78b`，与本问题无关，仅说明所用版本线）
- 该缺陷在 `13f32dd5` 上仍然存在（`research.ts:61-64`、`:84-86` 未变）

issue:58.body:
> Cross-tracking: [GitCode #101](https://gitcode.com/openJiuwen/sciencediscovery/issues/101) (Chinese counterpart of this issue).

### 🚀 Background Description

ScienceDiscovery already surfaces failures to the user — connection errors, 401/5xx request failures, settings save errors, panel render crashes, and Run/tool execution errors — via toasts, inline alerts, panel error boundaries, and Run summary text. Those surfaces currently offer only **Dismiss / Retry**. There is **no** way to copy the diagnostics that belong to that error, and **no** way to turn it into an issue from the same place.

What users actually have to do today:

1. The UI shows a short message such as `Request error: Unauthorized` or a panel `render failed`;
2. The useful evidence lives in rolling files under the data directory (default `.sciencediscovery-data/logs/` — `api.log`, `runner.log`, `run.log`). Many users do not know where that is or which slice to attach;
3. They leave the product, open GitCode or GitHub, fill a template by hand, and must remember to redact tokens, API keys, and session content.

Real failures therefore rarely become actionable issues. Maintainers get “it errored” without version, error code, run/request ids, or nearby log lines.

This request is a **user-facing feedback mechanism**, not another developer-only log sink. It complements the framework diagnostic-logging work ([GitHub #8](https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/issues/8), GitCode [#74](https://gitcode.com/openJiuwen/sciencediscovery/issues/74)): #8/#74 explicitly **do not** add a log viewer, search, or download UI. This issue is the missing “copy key logs + file an issue” path at the error itself.

### Design Ideas

On **user-visible errors**, add two actions (copy can be refined):

1. **Copy key diagnostics**: write a redacted, size-capped bundle to the clipboard. At minimum:
   - product version / build id;
   - OS and UI locale;
   - error title and body;
   - request / run / session ids when they exist;
   - the last few service-log lines related to this failure (reuse the redaction and length caps from #8/#74; do not copy whole log files).
2. **File an issue**: open the repository’s new-issue page with title and body prefilled from that bundle. GitCode (`openJiuwen/sciencediscovery`) is the canonical tracker; GitHub (`openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery`) is the public mirror — offer a GitHub link or a locale-based choice. The product must **not** create the issue on the user’s behalf and must **not** upload logs to a third party.

Priority error surfaces (can ship incrementally via one shared control):

- error toasts (`apps/web/src/Toasts.tsx` — dismiss only today);
- inline settings/dialog alerts (`apps/web/src/InlineErrorAlert.tsx` — dismiss only today);
- panel error boundaries (`apps/web/src/ErrorBoundary.tsx` — `label` + `message` only today);
- user-visible Run / tool failure text;
- CLI failures that have no equivalent Web surface.

**Alternatives considered**

- Copy-only, no “file issue” action: users still have to find the repo and the template.
- In-app form posting to a private backend: extra infra and auth, out of scope.
- Dumping full log files or unredacted session / tool payloads: leaks tokens, API keys, and research content.
- Silent crash telemetry: not part of this request.

**Open questions (need a product decision before implementation)**

- Whether “File an issue” defaults to GitCode or chooses GitCode vs GitHub from the UI locale;
- Whether the bundle is assembled in the client from the already-visible error plus version info, or via a local authenticated snapshot API (unredacted log files must not be exposed over HTTP).

### Involved Public APIs

- **User-visible behavior**: add Copy / File-issue actions on error controls; do not change the meaning of existing error copy.
- **HTTP**: if the client cannot see nearby log lines, a local authenticated read-only snapshot endpoint may return the redacted fields above. Do not expose `.sciencediscovery-data/logs/` as downloadable files, and do not add an anonymous public log download.
- **Issue hosts**: only open the public GitCode / GitHub “new issue” pages with prefilled content. Do not call their write APIs and do not embed a full issue editor.

### Description of Relevance to Other Modules

- Web error UI: toasts, inline alerts, error boundaries, Run summaries;
- `packages/operational-logging` and [GitHub #8](https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/issues/8) / [GitCode #74](https://gitcode.com/openJiuwen/sciencediscovery/issues/74): reuse existing redaction, rotation, and size caps;
- CLI: the same class of failure should yield a copyable diagnostics block;
- This does not replace the framework-internal events in #8/#74, and must not put user prompts, model I/O, or tool arguments/results into the bundle.

### Test Design and Test Plan

**Functional**

- [ ] Error toast, inline alert, and error boundary expose “Copy key diagnostics” in the failure state; the clipboard contains version + error body and does **not** contain access tokens / API keys / Bearer values;
- [ ] “File an issue” opens a new-issue URL for `openJiuwen/sciencediscovery` (and optionally the GitHub mirror) with title/body already carrying the error summary and diagnostics bundle;
- [ ] Dismissing the error does not upload logs or create an issue in the background;
- [ ] CLI user-visible failures print or otherwise provide an equivalent copyable diagnostics block (if CLI is in this slice).

**Security**

- [ ] The bundle uses the same redaction as #8/#74 (Authorization/Bearer, token, secret, password, cookie, URL userinfo);
- [ ] User prompts, tool arguments/results, and full stdout/stderr files are absent;
- [ ] Log excerpts and oversized error messages are truncated to an explicit cap.

**Engineering / user journey**

- [ ] Focused unit tests and Web control tests pass;
- [ ] User-journey E2E: induce a visible error → copy → assert clipboard → assert the “file issue” link opens with a complete prefilled body. Formal E2E must not use the human trial port 4310 or its fixed data directory.

### Additional Information

Code pointers (repo-relative, for implementers; not the acceptance surface):

- `apps/web/src/Toasts.tsx`
- `apps/web/src/InlineErrorAlert.tsx`
- `apps/web/src/ErrorBoundary.tsx`
- `apps/web/src/App.tsx` (request errors go to the top-right toast)
- Data-directory logs: `.sciencediscovery-data/logs/` (`api.log` / `runner.log` / `run.log`)

issue:665.body:
Implementation: ScienceDiscovery (ours) — PR follows within 24h. Do not pick up without a `pickup-ok` comment on this issue.

Written-by: ScienceDiscovery Product
Claimed-by: ScienceDiscovery Product
Claim-Id: df196a9b36e24084ad2fcd7ec43213c4
Branch: dev/665-bug-web-fetch-public-url-guard-misses-na
Base: 80ff50c18cdf
At: 2026-10-29T04:18:18Z

Implementation: ScienceDiscovery (ours) — do not pick up without a `pickup-ok` comment.

The public-URL gate for `web_fetch` now judges IPv4-mapped (`::ffff:a.b.c.d`) and IPv4-compatible (`::a.b.c.d`) literals by their embedded IPv4 (#662 / PR #664). Three other IPv6 forms that also carry an IPv4 address still pass, so the same model-supplied URL can reach loopback or the link-local metadata endpoint through them.

Verified on live main `a074172f60e5667e72ff04246316a0a41552cb46`, `packages/data-source/src/web/native/url-guard.ts`:

- NAT64 well-known prefix `64:ff9b::/96` — the IPv4 address sits in the last two hextets. `ipv6Blocked` only consults `ipv4Blocked` for the mapped/compatible forms (`url-guard.ts:58-68` on main; `:81-97` after #664), so `64:ff9b::...` falls to `return false` (`:68` on main, `:97` after #664).
- 6to4 `2002::/16` — the IPv4 address sits in hextets 2–3, which no branch inspects.
- IPv4-translated `::ffff:0:0:0/96` — 80 zero bits, then `ffff`, then 16 zero bits, then the IPv4 address; it matches neither the mapped test (`hextets[5] === 0xffff`) nor the compatible test (first six hextets zero) that #664 added at `url-guard.ts:95-97`.
- Deprecated site-local `fec0::/10` — the link-local branch tests `fe8`–`feb` only, so `fec0::/10` is reported public.

Current vs expected: `isBlockedAddress("64:ff9b::7f00:1")`, `"2002:7f00:1::"`, `"::ffff:0:7f00:1"` and `"fec0::1"` all return `false`; each must return `true`, and `assertPublicUrl("http://[64:ff9b::7f00:1]/")` and the two siblings must reject with `local and private network URLs are not allowed`. Decoding must stay narrow: `64:ff9b::808:808`, `2002:808:808::` and `::ffff:0:808:808` embed the public `8.8.8.8` and must keep returning `false` — a fix that rejects the whole prefix breaks NAT64 and 6to4 egress.

Suggested red test, in `packages/data-source/src/web/native/providers.test.ts`, next to `web_fetch refuses private and loopback targets`:

```ts
test("web_fetch judges NAT64, 6to4 and IPv4-translated literals by their embedded IPv4", () => {
  for (const address of ["64:ff9b::7f00:1", "2002:7f00:1::", "::ffff:0:7f00:1", "fec0::1"]) {
    assert.equal(isBlockedAddress(address), true, address);
  }
  for (const address of ["64:ff9b::808:808", "2002:808:808::", "::ffff:0:808:808"]) {
    assert.equal(isBlockedAddress(address), false, address);
  }
});
```

Run: `cd packages/data-source && node --import tsx --test src/web/native/providers.test.ts`

